h('5 Database Implementation')
p('Actual database behavior is hybrid by configuration. With MONGODB_URI, HospitalDatabase connects through Mongoose, creates indexes, seeds only missing foundation documents, loads collections into an in-memory data store per request, and persists diffs with bulkWrite/deleteMany. Without MONGODB_URI it loads/writes backend/storage/hospitalcare_db.json atomically via a temporary file and rename. The checked-in snapshot is the available local data file.')
p('The configuration contains SQL_DATABASE_TYPE and SQL_DATABASE_PATH defaults, but no SQL driver/package, SQL schema, or active SQL operations were found. Therefore a separate PostgreSQL/SQLite financial ledger is NOT IMPLEMENTED in the inspected source; bills and audit logs are part of the Mongo/JSON store.')
table(['Collection/domain entity','Key fields and relationships'],[['users','id, unique email, passwordHash, firebaseUid, role, active/lock/reset fields. Patient/doctor links use userId.'],['patients','patientCode, userId, demographics, contact, emergencyContact, assignedDoctorId, currentAdmissionId, identityKey.'],['doctors','doctorCode, userId, specialization, availability, assignedPatientIds.'],['wards','rooms[] and beds[] with status/current patient/admission; ward counts.'],['admissions','patientId, doctorId, ward/room/bed, status, discharge summary.'],['appointments','patientId, doctorId, date/slot/status; unique doctorSlotKey and patientSlotKey for active appointments.'],['medical_records / prescriptions','Clinical note or prescription attached to patientId and doctorId.'],['medical_documents','patientId, uploader identity/role, safeStorageKey, provider, MIME/size/category.'],['bills / insurance_claims / insurance_policies','Bill line items and calculated totals; claims link patientId + billId; policies link patientId.'],['audit_logs / notifications','Actor/action/resource trail and per-user notifications.'],['conversations / messages / teleconsultations','Participant/patient/doctor relationships and session join URL/status.']],[1.8,5.0])
p('User-specific data is managed by token-derived patientId/doctorId and requireResourceOwnership. Patients may address their own record; doctors must be assigned or have an appointment; administrators bypass ownership. Service list methods additionally filter data for a user role.')

h('6 Login and Authentication')
p('Patient self-registration is record claiming, not medical-record creation. POST /auth/patient-signup validates identifier, DOB, registered phone, email and strong password; AuthService.registerPatientAccount finds an existing record, confirms DOB/phone, rejects existing account/email, bcrypt-hashes the password (10 salt rounds), creates the patient user, links patient.userId, audits, and returns a JWT if Firebase is not configured.')
p('Login validates email/password, finds an active user, checks the account lock, uses bcrypt.compare, increments failed attempts, locks for 15 minutes after five failures (the sixth attempt sees 429), resets counts after success, attaches patientId/doctorId, audits, then either returns a JWT or links/uses a Firebase account. JWT contains id/email/role/fullName and relationship IDs; expiry defaults to 24h.')
p('When Firebase variables are configured, the frontend uses Firebase email/password and ID tokens; /auth/session establishes the backend profile. Auth middleware verifies a Firebase token, requires email verification except /me, /logout and /session, then falls back to local JWT during transition/testing. Logout adds the presented token to an in-memory revokedTokens Set and the client clears localStorage/signs out Firebase.')
bullets(['Password rules: at least 8 characters with uppercase, lowercase, number and special character.', 'Public /auth/register is wired but AuthService deliberately returns 410 REGISTRATION_MOVED; arbitrary-role public registration is blocked.', 'Forgot-password returns a success-like message for unknown email, but the current non-Firebase implementation returns the reset token in its response path. No email sender implementation was verified.', 'Important limitation: JWT revocation is process-local memory, so serverless/multi-instance revocation persistence is NOT VERIFIED.'])

h('7 Document Storage and File Management')
p('POST /api/documents/upload uses Multer memory storage. DocumentService validates the authenticated actor can act for the patient, file exists, is <= MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB (default 10 MB), has one of PDF/JPEG/PNG/WebP MIME types, has an allowed extension, and passes PDF/JPEG/PNG/WebP magic-byte verification. It generates a UUID-based safeStorageKey, writes bytes, then stores only metadata in medical_documents.')
p('Storage driver comes from STORAGE_DRIVER: local writes outside public assets at backend/storage/uploads by default; vercel-blob uses @vercel/blob and requires BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN. In production, STORAGE_DRIVER must be explicitly set and MongoDB must be configured unless ALLOW_EPHEMERAL_STORAGE=true.')
p('GET /documents/:id/download authorizes the actor, opens a local stream or Blob response, and returns content-disposition attachment. DELETE /documents/:id authorizes (admin or uploader) then deletes bytes through FileStorageService and removes metadata; operations are audit logged. GET document lists are role-filtered and patient lists use ownership checks.')

