h('14 Security and Error Handling')
bullets(['Helmet CSP/HSTS/frameguard/nosniff; restricted CORS origin logic; 10 MB request parser limits.', 'JWT/Firebase token authentication, active-account validation, role middleware, patient/doctor resource ownership checks and server-derived role context.', 'Bcrypt password hashes; strong password Zod rules; failed-login counter + 15-minute lock; auth and global IP rate limiting.', 'Multer memory buffering, MIME + extension + magic-byte checks, UUID keys outside public paths, authorized streams/deletion.', 'Zod validation for core mutating bodies; centralized AppError/errorHandler with request identifiers and no production stack trace response.', 'Mongo unique indexes for users, patient codes/identity key, doctor codes, admission/prescription/bill/claim codes and active appointment slot keys.', 'Audit events include actor/action/resource/status/IP/details; persistence middleware refreshes before request and persists successful mutations before response.'])
p('Caveats verified from code: the default JWT secret is embedded as a development fallback if the environment is missing; reset token handling is not backed by an email sender in inspected code; browser tokens are kept in localStorage; revocation Set is not shared/durable. These should be resolved for a real production healthcare deployment.')

